Proficiency in Python and C++ programming;

Knowledge of neural networks and familiarity with standard model architectures;

Hands-on experience with popular deep learning frameworks like PyTorch or TensorFlow;

Hands-on experience with common compiler frameworks for neural networks, such as MLIR or TVM;

Strong understanding of computer architecture alongside practical experience optimizing performance for targeted hardware;

Rapid prototyping capabilities for testing new ideas;

Strong interpersonal and communication skills.

Nice to have:

Experience with a machine learning compiler like IREE, ExecuTorch, ONNXRuntime, or similar compiler backend code generation experience (GCC, LLVM, etc.)

Experience with RISC-V architecture, especially the vector extension

Knowledge of digital/analog electrical circuits;

Knowledge of spike neural networks;

Knowledge of embedded platform and runtime;

Knowledge of graph algorithms, constraint solver, or heuristic algorithms.

Whether you’re passionate about microarchitecture, excited by verification or physical design, driven by supporting operations, building strong teams, or mastering the details of accounting, we’d love to hear from you!

